2. Landing remedy (lines 119-127, behaviour 7(e) lines 293-295): the chore-done command ends `git pull --ff-only origin master` while
   HEAD is still on chore/done-<id> (the kept leading `git switch chore/done-<id> &&`). After the squash-merge that pull is
   non-fast-forward. Probed: chore branch + squash merge on origin, `git pull --ff-only origin master` from the chore branch
   exits 128 "Not possible to fast-forward". The old script path fetched master:master and did not have this flaw, so the
   "plain gh and git path" is a regression for the done rung (the opus's own title item). The spec rung has the same
