W-128 spec sec red-team — Claude substitute (claude-sonnet-5-5), 2026-10-02, brief revision 1. SEC-SPEC: REVISE.
Brief: studio/briefs/W-128.md @32731ad (spec/W-128). Read-only; git probes ran in $TMPDIR repos (git 2.43.0). No bisellium verb run.

FINDINGS (blockers first)
1. HIGH — step 8 / residual 2 are false: a fast-forward silently destroys IGNORED files and dirs. Brief 99-101, 102-104, 380-381.
   Path: step 8 `status --porcelain --untracked-files=no` sees tracked changes only; step 9 `merge --ff-only <O>` then runs unpack_trees, which
   treats files matched by .gitignore as overwritable. Reproduced: ignored `ignored.cfg` holding local data, and ignored dir `node_modules/dep.js`,
   with an incoming commit that tracks a file of each name: merge exit 0, no warning, cfg overwritten, node_modules/ replaced by a file, data gone,
   status clean afterwards. Plain untracked (non-ignored) files are refused by git as the brief says; ignored ones are not. The brief's claim "handled by step 9" is wrong for this class.
   Fix: new step 8b before the merge: take the added paths `git diff --no-renames --name-only -z --diff-filter=A L O` and hold (reason contains `untracked`/`ignored`) if any
   is present on disk (lstat), has a non-directory ancestor on disk, or is an ancestor of an entry in `git ls-files -o -i --exclude-standard -z`. Add behaviour 5 rows:
   (g) ignored file at an incoming-added path, (h) ignored directory replaced by an incoming file; both byte-identical + hold, and retry succeeds after removal. Reword residual 2.
2. MEDIUM — "pinned object id" does not bind the move to a reviewed commit; the ff reaches arbitrary origin tip. Brief 87-88, 102-104, 369-374 (residual 1 overstates the guard).
   Path: O is read AFTER the fetch (step 4), so the pin only closes the 4->9 race; any descendant of L that origin serves (a push by anyone with write, a compromised origin) is
   checked out into the working tree. Tracked executable config rides along: .claude/settings.json hooks, package.json scripts, .github, agent files, i.e. code that runs on the
   next session in the main checkout with no human `git pull`. The old verb moved refs only. Worse, openPr (integrate.ts:284) calls fetchTrunk before any PR is merged, so the pr rung also ff's.
   Fix (prefer): `fetchTrunk(repo, target?)`; `landed` passes the already well-formed `pr.mergeOid`; require target ancestor-or-equal of O and merge exactly `target`, not O;
   with no target (pr rung) keep the old hold when behind. Alternative: state in residual 1 that the verb advances the checkout to the origin tip, unreviewed beyond branch protection, and have the Patron ruling cover it.
3. MEDIUM — failed step 9 leaves a half-updated tree, and the hold hides it. Brief 102-104, 5(a-e) 249-263 only test holds that mutate nothing.
   Reproduced: read-only subdirectory in the incoming change set: `merge --ff-only` exits 1 ("unable to unlink"), but other incoming files were already rewritten; HEAD unmoved,
   status shows ` M`, no MERGE_HEAD. The next fetchTrunk then holds `uncommitted` with no hint the verb caused it. A 120 s sh() timeout (integrate.ts:44) can do the same and strand index.lock.
   Fix: on non-zero or `r.error` at step 9, the reason ends `; the working tree may be partly updated: git -C <repo> status`. Add a behaviour 5 row (chmod a-w on a subdir; skip is NOT allowed under root, so use a directory/file collision instead of chmod if getuid()===0) asserting the reason text and that master did not move.
4. MEDIUM — nothing pins "no force/reset/pull/stash" or the literal-oid argument. Brief 106-108, 174-178, behaviours 3-5.
   `mutating()` (next.test.ts:678-692) does not recognise `git merge`, so the new main-checkout mutation is invisible to every ordered-calls pin; behaviours 3-5 call fetchTrunk in process with real git and no call log.
   Fix: in the rewritten b4 row assert from gitCalls (check BEFORE gitArgs strips -c): exactly one `merge`, argv `-c submodule.recurse=false merge -q --ff-only <40-hex equal to the origin tip>`, and no call among
   reset|pull|stash|checkout|switch|restore|clean, no `--force`/`-f`/`--update-head-ok`; extend mutating() with "git merge --ff-only". Without this a regression to `merge origin/master` or `pull` stays green.
5. LOW-MEDIUM — step 9 acts on HEAD, not on master. Brief 95-104.
   Path: holder identity is checked at step 2 and the merge runs minutes later (network fetch between). If the operator `git switch other` in that window, `merge --ff-only O` advances `other` when O descends from it;
   step 9's re-read of refs/heads/master then fails (hold) but `other` has already moved. Fix: immediately before step 9 require `symbolic-ref -q HEAD` === refs/heads/master (hold otherwise); keep the re-read.
6. LOW — Q3, parity-pin removal: no new blocker. Surviving verb guards (verified in next.test.ts): TERMINALS rows kept with `terminal` and `calls` (GHAS_STOP calls [] at :1184); refusals at :1387-1397 (alerts, API
   error, non-array); BLOCKED -> QUEUE_TIMEOUT at :1373; `-R`/`--json`/`--match-head-commit` reads at :1263-1275; unmatched() for any unscripted gh call. Gap: `gh` reached through a shell wrapper would pass.
   Fix (cheap): behaviour 2 row (d): integrate.ts has exactly one `spawnSync(` (inside `sh`), no `shell:`, `"bash"`, `exec(`, `execSync`. Also row (b) "SCRIPTS" must be case-sensitive or the :1248 title/comment "scripts" trips it; say so.

CLEARED (checked, no finding)
- Q2 `+` refspec: origin/master after step 3 is exactly what origin serves; L===O ok, O ancestor of L -> `ahead`, neither -> `diverged`, non-commit -> merge-base exit 128 -> hold. Rewind cannot move local master. Other readers of refs/remotes/origin/master: branch.ts:298-304 and opus-model.ts:903-906, both fail closed.
- Q1 ordering: O read (4) -> ancestry (7) -> literal 40-hex to merge (9); cannot start with `-`; ff-only itself rejects a HEAD that moved off an ancestor of O. Mid-merge MERGE_HEAD is not left by ff-only (checked). Assume-unchanged tracked edits: git refuses (checked). Symlinks in the incoming tree: git's leading-symlink check applies.
- Q4 regex: no path makes the rung complete without the id in the section; `(a (b))`, `(`, `Not Where...`, `)` after newline, NBSP all NO MATCH; `(a (b)` matches (harmless); \r\n matches (JS `$`); 200k-char tail runs in 0 ms (no ReDoS).
- Q5: warning is a fixed literal; treeHeader is `dirty:`+sha1 hex (shim sourceTree.ts:44-56); no injection.
- Q6: no live reference in .github/ci.yml, .claude/**, package.json, hooks, apps/, adapters/, examples/ (grep -r over whole tree minus studio/, dossier).

